WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.830 align:start position:0%
 
good morning  last friday i spoke with president  zielinski  to assess the situation in ukraine that  is created by russia's aggressive  actions  we discussed how the european union  could continue to support ukraine both  in the immediate and the medium term  and as ever the european union stands by  ukraine  in these difficult circumstances we are  very firm in our resolve  the european union has already provided  significant assistance to ukraine both  in the support of the country's  resilience and the country's  modernization but also specifically to  fight the covet-19 pandemic  since 2014 the european union and the  european financial institutions have  allocated over 17 billion  euros in grants and loans to the country  so today  i am announcing a new financial  assistance package to the country  made both of emergency loans and grants  first of all the commission proposes a  new emergency macro financial assistance  package of 1.2 billion euros  this package will help ukraine now  to address its financing needs due to  the conflict  we count on the council of the european  parliament to adopt this emergency macro  financial assistance as soon as possible  we will then proceed  to the rapid disbursement of the first  tranche of 600 million euros  we will soon start work  on a second larger macro financial  assistance program  to support the country's modernization  efforts  secondly the commission will almost  double its bilateral assistance to  ukraine in grants this year  another 120 million euros will be  allocated  this support will strengthen ukraine's  state building and resilience efforts  and finally on top of this we will  continue to invest in the country's  future  thanks to our investment plan for the  country the plan aims at leveraging over  6 billion euros in investment  and let me be clear once more  ukraine is a free and sovereign country  it makes its own choices  and the european union stands by the  side of ukraine thank you

